 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Find a big rock and stand right in the middle of the circle. The thunder won't scare us off the side of the hill, and we can see the storm coming. That gives you enough time to spot the exit and beat the lightning to it. Lighting often strikes the top of the hill just as the thunder gets loudest. Of course. A quiet little signal is enough. Yes, grab your sleeping bag and stand by the rock. The storm will pass in minutes. Find a big rock, lie down in the shelter of the hill, and wait it out. Lightening can sometimes jump to a tall object, so keep your head down. Good job. Lighten up and enjoy the rest of the hike. The storm will soon be behind us.",
